# ci_full_defconfig — the feature set every non-GCP CMake-configuring CI job
# resolves (the four Build & Test legs, Coverage, ThreadSanitizer, both
# Full-suite legs; coap-flake-measure.yml configures without any Kconfig
# flag, i.e. autodetect, and models the pre-#218 legs). "Full" means "every
# optional dependency the edhoc-feature CI image actually installs" — not
# every symbol y, and the difference is exactly what strict mode enforces.
#
# This file is written against `-DKYTHIRA_KCONFIG_STRICT=ON` (Requirement
# 5.1): a symbol set y whose dependency the image cannot satisfy is a
# configure FATAL_ERROR, so a dependency silently vanishing from the CI
# image fails fast instead of silently shrinking the test suite. That cuts
# both ways — a symbol enabled here that the image does NOT install would
# break every leg — which is why the exact set below is load-bearing in both
# directions.
#
# `default n` symbols deliberately NOT selected:
#
#   COVERAGE                — forcing it on would require Clang and
#                             CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug project-wide, breaking the
#                             g++-13 jobs that also apply this defconfig.
#                             Coverage is a separate build variant with its own
#                             CI job and its own -DENABLE_COVERAGE=ON.
#   ION_SERIALIZER          — ion-c comes from the opt-in `ion` vcpkg feature,
#                             and no CI job installs it (the main legs use
#                             --x-feature=edhoc only). Selecting it here would
#                             make a strict configure fail on an image that
#                             cannot satisfy it. Enable the vcpkg feature in
#                             ci.yml *first* if this is ever wanted.
#   COAP_TRANSPORT_LIBNYOCI — same shape: opt-in `coap-libnyoci` vcpkg feature,
#   COAP_TRANSPORT_CANTCOAP   and opt-in `coap-cantcoap`; neither is installed
#                             by any CI job.
#
# `default y` symbols explicitly turned OFF, because the edhoc-feature image
# does not install their dependency and under strict mode default-y would be
# a FATAL_ERROR (each was read off a green run's configure log — "not found",
# run 31569941823 — not inferred from vcpkg.json):
#
#   GCP_SDK, GCP_PRIVATECA  — google-cloud-cpp comes only from the opt-in
#                             `gcp` vcpkg feature, installed only by the GCP
#                             SDK Build job, which uses ci_gcp_defconfig (its
#                             own reconciliation of this same trade).
#   DNS_DISCOVERY           — libldns is in no CI image; the rfc1035/rfc2136
#                             discovery tests have never run in CI. Turning
#                             the symbol off records that honestly instead of
#                             leaving it to silent autodetect degradation.
#   POCO_DISCOVERY          — Poco DNSSD, same situation as libldns.
CONFIG_EDHOC=y
CONFIG_STDEXEC_BACKEND=y
CONFIG_BOOST_FUTURE_BACKEND=y
CONFIG_BOOST_BEAST_TRANSPORT=y
CONFIG_PROXYGEN_TRANSPORT=y
# Protobuf is always available — `grpc` is an unconditional vcpkg.json
# dependency and pulls it in — so unlike ion-c this is safe to select. It was
# missing from this list while CONFIG_PROTOBUF_SERIALIZER was inert (the
# feature enabled itself off the gRPC block's Protobuf_FOUND regardless), so
# the omission had no visible effect. Honouring the gate made it load-bearing.
CONFIG_PROTOBUF_SERIALIZER=y
# CONFIG_GCP_SDK is not set
# CONFIG_GCP_PRIVATECA is not set
# CONFIG_DNS_DISCOVERY is not set
# CONFIG_POCO_DISCOVERY is not set
